000100 IDENTIFICATION DIVISION.
000200 PROGRAM-ID. SEQUPD.
000300* OPEN I-O and REWRITE on a plain sequential file. On MVS this is
000400* QSAM's own update mode -- OPEN UPDAT, GET in locate mode, PUTX --
000500* not BSAM. QSAM hands back a pointer into its buffer and puts the
000600* block back where it came from, so blocking and a short last block
000700* are the access method's problem rather than the compiler's.
000800*
000900* The file is written BLOCK CONTAINS 3 RECORDS with six records in
001000* it, so the rewrites straddle a block boundary: records 2 and 4
001100* sit in different blocks, and record 5 is rewritten FROM working
001200* storage in the second block after record 4 forced the first one
001300* out. If PUTX were writing the wrong block, that is where it shows.
001400 ENVIRONMENT DIVISION.
001500 INPUT-OUTPUT SECTION.
001600 FILE-CONTROL.
001700     SELECT OUT-FILE ASSIGN TO UT-S-UPDFILE.
001800     SELECT UPD-FILE ASSIGN TO UT-S-UPDFILE.
001900     SELECT IN-FILE  ASSIGN TO UT-S-UPDFILE.
002000 DATA DIVISION.
002100 FILE SECTION.
002200 FD  OUT-FILE
002300     BLOCK CONTAINS 3 RECORDS
002400     LABEL RECORDS ARE STANDARD.
002500 01  OUT-REC      PIC X(20).
002600 FD  UPD-FILE
002700     LABEL RECORDS ARE STANDARD.
002800 01  UPD-REC.
002900     02  U-HEAD   PIC X(10).
003000     02  U-TAIL   PIC X(10).
003100 FD  IN-FILE
003200     LABEL RECORDS ARE STANDARD.
003300 01  IN-REC       PIC X(20).
003400 WORKING-STORAGE SECTION.
003500 01  EOF-FLAG     PIC X     VALUE 'N'.
003600 01  CTR          PIC 99    VALUE 0.
003700 01  WS-LINE      PIC X(20).
003800 01  WS-FROM      PIC X(20) VALUE 'RECORD 05 FROM-WS   '.
003900 PROCEDURE DIVISION.
004000     OPEN OUTPUT OUT-FILE.
004100     MOVE 'RECORD 01 ORIGINAL  ' TO OUT-REC.
004200     WRITE OUT-REC.
004300     MOVE 'RECORD 02 ORIGINAL  ' TO OUT-REC.
004400     WRITE OUT-REC.
004500     MOVE 'RECORD 03 ORIGINAL  ' TO OUT-REC.
004600     WRITE OUT-REC.
004700     MOVE 'RECORD 04 ORIGINAL  ' TO OUT-REC.
004800     WRITE OUT-REC.
004900     MOVE 'RECORD 05 ORIGINAL  ' TO OUT-REC.
005000     WRITE OUT-REC.
005100     MOVE 'RECORD 06 ORIGINAL  ' TO OUT-REC.
005200     WRITE OUT-REC.
005300     CLOSE OUT-FILE.
005400*
005500     OPEN I-O UPD-FILE.
005600     MOVE 0 TO CTR.
005700     MOVE 'N' TO EOF-FLAG.
005800 UPD-LOOP.
005900     READ UPD-FILE AT END MOVE 'Y' TO EOF-FLAG.
006000     IF EOF-FLAG = 'Y' GO TO UPD-DONE.
006100     ADD 1 TO CTR.
006200     IF CTR = 2 GO TO UPD-CHANGE.
006300     IF CTR = 4 GO TO UPD-CHANGE.
006400     IF CTR = 5 GO TO UPD-FROM.
006500     GO TO UPD-LOOP.
006600 UPD-CHANGE.
006700     MOVE 'CHANGED   ' TO U-TAIL.
006800     REWRITE UPD-REC.
006900     GO TO UPD-LOOP.
007000 UPD-FROM.
007100     REWRITE UPD-REC FROM WS-FROM.
007200     GO TO UPD-LOOP.
007700 UPD-DONE.
007800     CLOSE UPD-FILE.
007900*
008000     OPEN INPUT IN-FILE.
008100     MOVE 'N' TO EOF-FLAG.
008200 IN-LOOP.
008300     READ IN-FILE AT END MOVE 'Y' TO EOF-FLAG.
008400     IF EOF-FLAG = 'Y' GO TO IN-DONE.
008500     MOVE IN-REC TO WS-LINE.
008600     DISPLAY '[' WS-LINE ']'.
008700     GO TO IN-LOOP.
008800 IN-DONE.
008900     CLOSE IN-FILE.
009000     STOP RUN.
